# MANUAL IMAGE LAW — FACE CARDS + TOP INTERNALS

**Status: MANDATORY · NON-NEGOTIABLE.** Owner locked 2026-07-12 (said ~100×).

## The job (every pillar)

For **each** Q&A entry you must **literally open / handle that entry yourself** and do:

1. **Face card** — clean photo, **no baked title / no old terrible font**
2. **Top internal image** — clean photo replacing bad/missing/pollinations junk

That is **~N × 2** per pillar (e.g. Industry KPIs ≈ **670 × 2**). Dupes **OK** on top internals only. Face/bank photos stay unique.

## HARD BAN — no “run a thing to do it for you”

Agents **MUST NOT**:

- Launch a batch / daemon / “fast bank” / `fillEntryMissingImages` / `repairBrokenQaImages` / pollinations rewrite / any unsupervised script that **replaces faces or top internals across many entries**
- Pre-approve / auto-keep / auto-swap an entire pillar’s faces or top internals
- Declare a pillar’s images “done” because a counter hit N/N from a script

**It will not work** unless you are **manually doing them 1 by 1**. Owner will catch cuts.

## What “manual 1-by-1” means

- Go **into each entry** (blob / live page / review room card for **that** id)
- Choose / pull / place **that** entry’s face and **that** entry’s top internal yourself
- Visually confirm: no yellow outlined title bake, no pollinations left in the top internal slot, image actually renders
- Then move to the **next** id — serial, not fire-and-forget

Helpers (Pexels search, file write, blob set for **the current id**) are fine **while you are on that one entry**. Unsupervised multi-id replacement is not.

## Bypass

Immutable. Override **only** with owner passcode **`4444`**.  
No other excuse (speed, “dupes OK”, “already 676/676”, pre-draft waiting, next pillar, IndexNow, etc.).

## After both passes

Review → pre-draft → publish → next pillar. Still no lazy corners.

